            "note": "Coefficients of $P(q^2)F(q^2)=\\sum_{n=0}^3 a_n z^n$ for $A_0$, $A_1$, $A_2$ and $V$, from the continuum extrapolation to the physical $b$ mass (Table XVI). $P(q^2)=\\prod z(q^2,M_\\mathrm{pole}^2)$ collects three $0^-$, four $1^-$ and four $1^+$ $B_c$ poles (Table XV) with no outer functions, so these are not BGL coefficients. $z=z(q^2,t_0)$ with $t_0=t_-$, $t_+=(M_H+M_{D^*})^2$ and $H$ an $h\\bar u$ pseudoscalar. The $16\\times16$ correlation matrix is assembled from the ten block matrices in Appendix A. The kinematic constraint $2M_{J/\\psi}A_0(0)=(M_{J/\\psi}+M_{H_c})A_1(0)-(M_{J/\\psi}-M_{H_c})A_2(0)$ is imposed through a nuisance term, leaving the matrix with a near-zero eigenvalue. Rates, branching fractions and $|V_{cb}|$ are not stored.",
